TASK-260720-14jjgt,task,compiled-skill-authoring-guide,Publish the portable compiled-skill authoring guide,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,"Publish a practical implementation-neutral guide for authors of schema v6 Go command skills, building on the normative schema and CLI documentation without asking authors to infer portability rules from manager source.","Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-3lo9jc and TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own docs/compiled-skill-authoring.md plus its README and conformance navigation links. Reuse canonical terms and link the exact schema, fixture, build-driver vectors, and conformance guide. Cover both manifest spellings only where compatibility requires it. Do not promise manager support before release, document physical cache paths as portable, add package-selected build options, or duplicate implementation-specific troubleshooting.","The guide contains a complete valid schema v6 manifest and matching repository tree for the shared minimal Go fixture. It states trusted Go 1.23-or-newer allowlisted toolchain requirements, native target only, vendor consistency, main-package and build-root rules, disabled cgo, PGO, workspaces, downloads, toolchain switching, external linking, generators, plugins, and output execution during install. It explains prompt-context and runtime exclusion, cache miss, verified hit, corrupt or untrusted rebuild, logical portable key and receipt fields versus implementation-specific storage, compiler-free dry-run, status and repair behavior, command launch and argument or exit propagation, and the protected-state trust boundary. It lists resource and compiler-input denial-of-service limits honestly, links the shared cases, labels unreleased support accurately, passes link and documentation validation, and contains no release claim or pin change.","[""TASK-260720-2g7avf"",""TASK-260720-3lo9jc""]","[""TASK-260720-3pvihp"",""TASK-260720-22ynoi""]","[{""text"":""Document a complete schema v6 fixture tree and manifest with exact go-v1 prerequisites"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Document context isolation, cache and receipt semantics, dry-run, launch, repair, limits, and trust boundaries"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Verify links and documentation without claiming unreleased support or portable physical cache paths"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:22:34Z,true,[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-14jjgt_source-contract.md"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-14jjgt/TASK-260720-14jjgt_source-contract.md"",""description"":""Authoring-guide source and ownership boundaries""}]",[]
TASK-260720-1673lr,task,curator-shared-build-suite-consumer,Consume the shared compiled-build suite in Curator,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Add an independent Go consumer for every shared compiled-build interoperability case. The consumer must exercise Curator behavior against the external suite root and derive no expected values from csk or from implementation-local fixtures.,"Work in the Curator repository after the Curator Go build-driver conformance handoff and TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own internal/interop/compiled_build_test.go and narrowly related test-only helpers, using CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT. Exercise real manifest parsing, install planning, build and cache behavior, shim launch, argument and exit propagation, and rejection ordering in isolated temporary homes and projects. Extend the existing rc.4 vector consumer rather than replacing it. Do not call or import csk, copy shared vectors into the repository, weaken no-skip behavior, or change the curator-spec CI pin in this task.","With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Go consumer enumerates every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, or skipped case IDs. The positive fixture installs from the unmodified suite, excludes build roots from context and runtime copies, builds on a miss, reuses a verified cache entry, performs a compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run, and launches the installed command with the exact shared stdout, stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no implementation-owned expected outcome or binary hash is introduced. The focused external-suite tests and go test ./... pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when the environment variable is absent.","[""TASK-260720-2g7avf"",""TASK-260720-jrrgw9""]","[""TASK-260720-3nj1r6""]","[{""text"":""Enumerate every external compiled-build case exactly once with no implementation-local oracle"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Exercise real Curator install, cache, dry-run, rejection, shim launch, arguments, streams, and exit status"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run focused external-suite tests and go test ./... with isolated state and no suite-present skips"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:28:46Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-1utsx8,task,audit-csk-released-suite-pin,Audit the csk released-suite pin and CI gate,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Verify that the csk implementation story advances its protocol-suite pin only to the qualified released schema v6 revision and that the compiled-build consumer is a required cross-platform gate. Apply only narrowly scoped CI corrections if the handoff diverges.,"Work in csk after TASK-260720-25d05o and the csk integrated verification task. Audit .github/workflows/ci.yml, every curator-spec checkout ref, the compiled-build conformance invocation, and any directly related no-skip guard. Candidate-phase testing may use an explicitly supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT but must leave the committed release pin at the previous released suite. The eventual pin must equal the exact immutable protocol release commit recorded by TASK-260720-25d05o. Do not use a branch, mutable tag, feature-worktree SHA, guessed future release, or Curator implementation detail.","Every csk CI job that supplies CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT resolves the same qualified full curator-spec release commit and pin history shows that it moved only after TASK-260720-25d05o evidence existed. Linux, macOS, and Windows across the supported Python matrix install the supported Go toolchain and execute the full Python suite consumer with no compiled-build case skipped, xfailed, duplicated, or silently filtered. The focused protocol test, full pytest suite, and strict type check pass against the released suite, existing schema 1 through 5 coverage remains active, and a negative CI guard detects an old suite that lacks compiled-build cases. Any correction is limited to CI or test-gate wiring and the outcome records exact refs and CI links without fabricating a claim.","[""TASK-260720-25d05o"",""TASK-260720-3s27te""]","[""TASK-260720-22ynoi""]","[{""text"":""Use only the qualified released curator-spec commit in every csk suite checkout"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Require the full compiled-build consumer with no skip or xfail on Linux, macOS, and Windows"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run focused protocol, full pytest, and strict typing validation while preserving legacy schema coverage"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:30:54Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-22ynoi,task,verify-cross-manager-build-interop,Verify compiled-build interoperability across released implementations,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,"Perform an independent acceptance audit of the released protocol suite, both manager consumers, cross-platform parity evidence, author documentation, and pin provenance. Produce evidence only; substantive defects return to the owning task.","Run after the shared cases, consumers, runner, documents, evidence qualification, and all three release-safe pin promotions. Use clean checkouts at the exact qualified refs. Run curator-spec validation and deterministic regeneration checks, the focused and full Curator tests, the focused and full csk tests, and the black-box runner locally where supported; verify required Linux, macOS, and Windows CI records for the full matrix. Inspect diffs for copied expected values and premature pins. Attach a task-scoped coverage and provenance report; do not alter product behavior or manufacture unavailable platform results.","The report maps every story acceptance criterion to a passing command, shared case ID, document section, or immutable CI record. Both managers consume the byte-identical suite digest, enumerate the identical case set without skips or xfails, reject every shared negative case in the same normalized class and boundary, and install then launch the same fixture behavior with matching forwarded arguments, stdout, stderr, and exit status. Dry-run, cache miss, verified hit, corrupt or untrusted rebuild, context exclusion, rollback, and no-package-code-before-user-launch outcomes match. The author guide contains the complete schema v6 example, prerequisites, cache semantics, security limits, and portability caveats; the matrix and future-driver process are complete and name unsafe build-system non-goals. Pin history proves no rc.4 suite or manager ref moved before real release qualification, no release evidence is inferred from local work, all relevant repository validation commands pass, and any substantive divergence is reported against its owning task rather than normalized away.","[""TASK-260720-38l1sy"",""TASK-260720-1utsx8"",""TASK-260720-vs6den"",""TASK-260720-14jjgt"",""TASK-260720-p7sdhg""]",[],"[{""text"":""Attach exact command and immutable CI evidence for spec, Curator, csk, and cross-manager parity"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Map every acceptance criterion, negative cluster, cache and dry-run outcome, and documentation requirement"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Audit suite identity, no-copy independence, no skips, and release-safe pin history across all repositories"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:11:43Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-25d05o,task,qualify-protocol-release-evidence,Qualify the released schema v6 protocol suite,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Establish a second immutable evidence gate after released manager revisions pass the in-tree specification workflow and before Curator or csk advances its protocol-suite pin.,"Perform a read-only qualification after TASK-260720-vs6den and the actual curator-spec schema v6 release. Resolve the annotated signed release tag to its full commit, verify the published conformance archive and checksum against the repository suite manifest, and collect required specification CI including both pinned managers and the black-box parity gate. Attach a task-scoped evidence record. Do not edit manager workflows, suite pins, claims, tags, release notes, checksums, or artifacts. A release candidate plan, branch, mutable tag, local archive, or successful pre-release workflow is not a published protocol release.","The outcome records the actual protocol version and tag, full commit ID, release URL and timestamp, tag or artifact signature result required by governance, conformance archive checksum, generated suite SHA-256, and passing required Linux, macOS, and Windows implementation-conformance records. The archive suite is byte-identical to the tagged repository suite and its manifest includes the compiled-build fixture and cases. Curator and csk refs in the release gate match TASK-260720-3pvihp and pass without skipped or xfailed compiled-build cases. No manager suite pin changed before this qualification. If the release, signature, artifact, digest, or CI evidence is missing or inconsistent, the task records the exact missing external item and transitions to blocked without guessing a ref or fabricating conformance evidence.","[""TASK-260720-vs6den""]","[""TASK-260720-38l1sy"",""TASK-260720-1utsx8""]","[{""text"":""Verify the published signed protocol tag, full commit, release artifacts, checksums, and suite digest"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Verify released-suite parity CI for both qualified managers on Linux, macOS, and Windows with no skips"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach qualification evidence or block with the exact missing release item before any manager suite pin moves"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:10:35Z,2026-07-20T02:11:43Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-2g7avf,task,shared-compiled-build-interop-cases,Define shared executable compiled-build interoperability cases,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,"Extend curator-spec with a manager-neutral executable interoperability layer that reuses the protocol-owned schema v6 Go fixture and normative build and lifecycle vectors. The shared suite is the only owner of inputs and expected outcomes, so Curator and csk remain independent consumers rather than copies of one another.","Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-1s1vr6 and TASK-260720-cw39jh. Extend the exact Go fixture path landed by TASK-260720-1s1vr6 rather than adding a second fixture. Own conformance/v1/vectors/compiled-build-interop.json, its generator and tests in tools/generate-vectors, and conformance/v1/manifest.json inventory. Define portable install, build, cache-hit, dry-run, and launch cases plus references to the complete shared negative corpus. Do not duplicate schema or lifecycle vectors, compare platform-dependent binary bytes, prescribe manager-home paths, import implementation packages, or update release pins.","The shared case file has stable case IDs and records the fixture path, operation, expected normalized outcome, expected persistent-mutation class, expected compiler-process class, and launch stdout, stderr, and exit behavior where applicable. The complete schema v6 fixture contains one build_roots entry, one go-v1 main command, a vendored dependency, a transitive embedded input, unrelated prompt context, and deterministic argument forwarding plus a nonzero-exit mode. Cases prove build roots never enter prompt context or runtime copying, dry-run launches no source-aware Go command and mutates nothing, cache hit launches the same installed command behavior, and cache miss builds then launches only on explicit user invocation. Every build-drivers and compiled manager-lifecycle negative case is included directly or referenced by stable ID with the same expected rejection class. The generator imports no manager code, regeneration is byte-stable, existing script fixture values remain unchanged, and make validate plus make regenerate-check pass.","[""TASK-260720-cw39jh""]","[""TASK-260720-1673lr"",""TASK-260720-31zeo2"",""TASK-260720-14jjgt""]","[{""text"":""Generate stable executable case IDs and expected normalized outcomes from curator-spec only"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Cover install, cache, dry-run, launch, context exclusion, and the complete shared negative corpus"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run generator tests, make validate, and deterministic regeneration checks without changing legacy fixture values"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:22:34Z,true,[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-2g7avf_independent-consumers.puml"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-2g7avf/TASK-260720-2g7avf_independent-consumers.puml"",""description"":""Component source defining suite ownership and independent consumer boundaries""},{""name"":""TASK-260720-2g7avf_source-contract.md"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-2g7avf/TASK-260720-2g7avf_source-contract.md"",""description"":""Authoritative design and upstream artifact ownership""}]","[{""name"":""TASK-260720-2g7avf_independent-consumers.svg"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-2g7avf/TASK-260720-2g7avf_independent-consumers.svg"",""description"":""Rendered independent-consumer component diagram""}]"
TASK-260720-31zeo2,task,csk-shared-build-suite-consumer,Consume the shared compiled-build suite in csk,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Add an independent Python consumer for every shared compiled-build interoperability case. The consumer must exercise csk behavior against the external suite root and derive no expected values from Curator or from implementation-local fixtures.,"Work in the csk repository after the csk shared-vector and real-Go end-to-end handoffs plus TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own the compiled-build additions to tests/test_protocol_conformance.py and narrowly related test-only helpers, using CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT. Exercise real manifest parsing, install planning, build and cache behavior, shim launch, argument and exit propagation, and rejection ordering in isolated temporary homes and projects. Extend the existing rc.4 vector consumer rather than replacing it. Do not call or import Curator, copy shared vectors into the repository, weaken no-skip behavior, or change the curator-spec CI pin in this task.","With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Python consumer parametrizes every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, xfailed, or skipped case IDs. The positive fixture installs from the unmodified suite, excludes build roots from context and runtime copies, builds on a miss, reuses a verified cache entry, performs a compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run including audit-registry state, and launches the installed command with the exact shared stdout, stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no implementation-owned expected outcome or binary hash is introduced. The focused external-suite tests, full pytest suite, and strict type check pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when the environment variable is absent.","[""TASK-260720-2g7avf"",""TASK-260720-12r55p""]","[""TASK-260720-3nj1r6""]","[{""text"":""Parametrize every external compiled-build case exactly once with no implementation-local oracle"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Exercise real csk install, cache, dry-run, rejection, shim launch, arguments, streams, and exit status"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run focused external-suite tests, full pytest, and strict type checking with no suite-present skip or xfail"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:30:54Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-38l1sy,task,audit-curator-released-suite-pin,Audit the Curator released-suite pin and CI gate,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Verify that the Curator implementation story advances its protocol-suite pin only to the qualified released schema v6 revision and that the compiled-build consumer is a required cross-platform gate. Apply only narrowly scoped CI corrections if the handoff diverges.,"Work in Curator after TASK-260720-25d05o and the Curator cross-platform CI task. Audit .github/workflows/ci.yml, every curator-spec checkout ref, the compiled-build conformance invocation, and any directly related no-skip guard. Candidate-phase testing may use an explicitly supplied CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT but must leave the committed release pin at the previous released suite. The eventual pin must equal the exact immutable protocol release commit recorded by TASK-260720-25d05o. Do not use a branch, mutable tag, feature-worktree SHA, guessed future release, or csk implementation detail.","Every Curator CI job that supplies CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT resolves the same qualified full curator-spec release commit and pin history shows that it moved only after TASK-260720-25d05o evidence existed. Linux, macOS, and Windows install the supported Go toolchain and execute the full Go suite consumer with no compiled-build case skipped, duplicated, or silently filtered. The focused interop job and go test ./... pass against the released suite, existing schema 1 through 5 coverage remains active, and a negative CI guard detects an old suite that lacks compiled-build cases. Any correction is limited to CI or test-gate wiring and the outcome records exact refs and CI links without fabricating a claim.","[""TASK-260720-25d05o"",""TASK-260720-1pvfj5""]","[""TASK-260720-22ynoi""]","[{""text"":""Use only the qualified released curator-spec commit in every Curator suite checkout"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Require the full compiled-build consumer with no skips on Linux, macOS, and Windows"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run focused interop and full Go validation while preserving all legacy schema coverage"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:30:54Z,true,[],[],[]
TASK-260720-3nj1r6,task,cross-manager-interop-runner,Run both managers through one black-box interoperability gate,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Add a curator-spec-owned runner that invokes the two independent conformance entrypoints against the same immutable suite root and compares their normalized case results without importing either implementation.,"Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-1673lr and TASK-260720-31zeo2. Own tools/run_compiled_build_interop.py, tools/test_run_compiled_build_interop.py, and the corresponding execution section in conformance/README.md. Accept explicit Curator and csk checkout or executable paths plus the suite root; create separate temporary manager homes, projects, caches, and fixture copies; emit one machine-readable result record per case. The suite remains the oracle. Do not embed manager refs, release pins, copied expected values, implementation-specific cache layouts, or cross-manager code imports.","The runner validates the suite manifest before execution, invokes each manager consumer with the identical suite bytes, and rejects missing, extra, duplicate, skipped, xfailed, timed-out, or crashed cases. Its normalization removes only declared transport differences such as temporary absolute paths and platform executable suffixes; acceptance or rejection class, build or no-build boundary, mutation class, launch stdout and stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status remain comparable. The two managers run in disjoint state roots and never consume one another’s cache or artifacts. A JSON report identifies suite digest, implementation identities supplied by the caller, per-case outcomes, and parity verdict without claiming release conformance. Unit tests inject divergent, missing, skipped, timeout, and malformed result streams and prove the runner fails closed. The documented local command succeeds against qualified checkouts and curator-spec validation remains green.","[""TASK-260720-1673lr"",""TASK-260720-31zeo2""]","[""TASK-260720-3pvihp""]","[{""text"":""Implement isolated black-box execution and strict machine-readable result collection for both consumers"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Compare full case identity, normalized outcome, mutation boundary, and launch behavior without hiding decisions"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Test malformed, divergent, missing, skipped, crashed, and timed-out consumer results fail closed"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:31:22Z,true,[],[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-3nj1r6_interop-plan.md"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-3nj1r6/TASK-260720-3nj1r6_interop-plan.md"",""description"":""Implementation-ready ownership, result envelope, isolation, scenario, and release-order contract""}]"
TASK-260720-3pvihp,task,qualify-manager-release-evidence,Qualify manager releases for the specification gate,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Establish a hard evidence gate between successful candidate interoperability tests and any change to curator-spec implementation pins.,"Perform a read-only qualification after protocol v6 candidate verification, both manager consumers, the black-box runner, and downstream documents are accepted. Resolve the published Curator and csk release tags to full immutable commits and bind them to the exact committed curator-spec candidate suite digest they passed. Attach a task-scoped evidence record. Do not edit workflows, pins, claims, tags, changelogs, or release assets. A working tree, branch name, mutable tag, local-only unrecorded pass, board status, planned version, or future commit is not release evidence. The protocol itself need not be released yet because this gate exists to qualify released manager revisions for the in-tree specification release gate.","The outcome records each actual manager release version or tag, full commit ID, release URL and timestamp, released artifact identity where applicable, the exact committed curator-spec candidate revision and suite SHA-256 tested, and reproducible passing consumer plus black-box results. Both manager releases consume the byte-identical candidate suite and every referenced commit exists in its public repository. The report states that this is pre-release protocol evidence, emits no conformance claim v2, and confirms that no implementation pin changed before qualification. If either manager release or exact-suite test evidence is absent, the task records the exact missing external item, recommends no pin movement, and transitions to blocked rather than substituting a branch, guessed hash, local worktree commit, or fabricated claim.","[""TASK-260720-3nj1r6"",""TASK-260720-14jjgt"",""TASK-260720-p7sdhg"",""TASK-260720-3ag6pi""]","[""TASK-260720-vs6den""]","[{""text"":""Record actual published versions, full commits, suite digest, artifacts, and required CI evidence"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Reject branches, mutable tags, local-only passes, future hashes, and board status as release evidence"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach the qualification record or block with the exact missing external release evidence and no pin edits"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:17:31Z,true,[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-3pvihp_release-evidence-gates.puml"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-3pvihp/TASK-260720-3pvihp_release-evidence-gates.puml"",""description"":""Activity source defining release evidence and pin promotion ordering""}]","[{""name"":""TASK-260720-3pvihp_release-evidence-gates.svg"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-3pvihp/TASK-260720-3pvihp_release-evidence-gates.svg"",""description"":""Rendered release-evidence gate activity diagram""}]"
TASK-260720-p7sdhg,task,language-driver-admission-matrix,Define the language-driver matrix and admission gate,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,Turn the accepted build-system research into a maintained language and toolchain matrix plus a normative-quality checklist for proposing future compile-only driver revisions.,"Work in curator-spec after the compile-only decision and TASK-260720-3lo9jc. Own docs/build-driver-admission.md plus its README and decision-record navigation links. Classify Go, Rust and Cargo, Zig, Swift and SwiftPM, direct C and C++ compilers, Make, CMake, Meson, Java and Kotlin build paths, .NET and MSBuild, Node and TypeScript compilers and bundlers, Deno, and Python packaging. Do not reserve speculative driver identifiers, imply that offline equals safe, or weaken the closed go-v1 contract.","The matrix uses explicit supported-now, deferred-for-separate-design, and prohibited-without-a-separate-sandboxed-driver classes with a concise security rationale for every listed ecosystem. Make, CMake, Meson, Cargo build scripts and procedural macros, SwiftPM manifests and plugins, Maven and Gradle plugins, MSBuild tasks and generators, npm lifecycle scripts, bundler configs and plugins, Python build backends, and any generic shell or package-provided argv are named non-goals. The future-driver process requires a new versioned identifier, threat-model review, closed schema, manager-owned executable and argv graph, source and dependency identity, toolchain and target fingerprint, context isolation, cache and receipt model, dry-run semantics, resource limits, positive and negative vectors, authoring docs, two independent consumers, cross-platform parity evidence, compatibility and security review, and an immutable release. Links resolve, the accepted research remains traceable, and no future support or release evidence is fabricated.","[""TASK-260720-3lo9jc""]","[""TASK-260720-3pvihp"",""TASK-260720-22ynoi""]","[{""text"":""Classify every required language and build ecosystem with security rationale"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Name unsafe build systems and package-controlled hooks, plugins, configs, and argv as explicit non-goals"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Define the complete future-driver admission checklist and preserve traceability to accepted research"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:22:34Z,true,[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-p7sdhg_source-contract.md"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-p7sdhg/TASK-260720-p7sdhg_source-contract.md"",""description"":""Accepted language matrix and future-driver baseline""}]",[]
TASK-260720-vs6den,task,promote-spec-implementation-pins,Promote curator-spec implementation pins after manager releases,backlog,STORY-260720-21bsr2,,"Advance curator-spec implementation conformance pins only to the qualified released Curator and csk revisions, then make the shared black-box parity gate part of the specification CI matrix.","Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-3pvihp and the two manager-side pin promotions. Own only the Curator and csk refs and their compiled-build invocations in the implementation-conformance workflow plus the cross-manager runner step. Preserve the registry-service pin unless its own released contract requires a change. Do not use branches, mutable tags, candidate worktree commits, or implementation-owned expected values.","The workflow pins Curator and csk by the exact full commits recorded in release qualification and each commit is traceable to a published release. On Linux, macOS, and Windows it supplies the in-tree released suite to both consumers, installs the supported Go and Python toolchains, rejects any skip or xfail, and runs the black-box runner against isolated manager state. The gate fails for missing case IDs, normalized outcome divergence, launch stdout or stderr or exit mismatch, or changed negative-case rejection boundaries. Existing registry-service coverage remains intact, action pins remain immutable, and no implementation pin is advanced before its recorded release evidence.","[""TASK-260720-3pvihp""]","[""TASK-260720-25d05o"",""TASK-260720-22ynoi""]","[{""text"":""Pin only the qualified released Curator and csk commits in curator-spec implementation CI"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run both consumers and the isolated parity runner on Linux, macOS, and Windows with no skips"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Preserve registry coverage and fail on any case-set, outcome-boundary, or launch-behavior divergence"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T02:06:02Z,2026-07-20T02:11:43Z,true,[],[],[]

